They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
Sometime in the bright morning, often in mid-day,
And oft in the fierce gale like to-day,
Make deep groans and groan aloud to heaven
If unseen heaven did judge that time well,
Which thou dost thank for, being far off.
To tell that, we behold heaven through thine eyes;
A still clearer sight than doth heaven show
When thou art but third star in the firmament.
  But, sad as I am at thy pain, thy doom is thine:
  I seek a cure which cannot be found.


