That she might think me some untutored youth,
Riding on a stone that no motion buries,
Now looks polished with jewels daily put.
Therefore I say, "Thou art old," that gives me pleasure in her sweet song,
But if I take offense for falsehood,
I change my purpose and say, "She loves true."
