For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
For how gladly truth drinks,
Whilst in you lies the foul.
For of thy worth there is no debate;
No worth in this world doth love esteem,
And to love this world doth him subsist.
Yet 'tis well that me, most hated of my friends,
Do more praise of thee than of my friend;
Thou see'st through all my digressions,
Till I have brought myself like to his.
  So by this love myself untainted show,
  My deserting love that thou maintainest.



